====Verb====
{{en-verb|++}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[kidnap]] a [[cat]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1990 |title=Kalliope |author=|page=40 |ISBN=|passage=When you suspect your cat's up a tree because he was chased or now locked up in the parked car because someone conspired to '''catnap''' him (he is quite the personality), what economic scales could they employ to set ransom? }}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2002| chapter=A Man Wanted to Buy a Cat| author=Joseph Ashby Porter | title=Touch Wood: Short Stories |editor=| page=12| passage=The man thought, if she refuses, I could '''catnap''' it early one Wednesday afternoon while she's dozing. Leave a bogus ransom note?.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2018  |title='''Catnapped'''!|author=Elaine Viets |page= |ISBN=|passage=But the jury was appalled that Amber had stepped over Mort's dead body to steal his cat, and moved by Trish's dignified and heartrending testimony about her suffering when Justine was '''catnapped'''.}}
#* {{quote-video game|en|date=30 October 2019|title=w:Luigi's Mansion 3|developer=w:Next Level Games|publisher=w:Nintendo|version=1.4.0|level=Main Observation Room (15F: Master Suite)|text=''Hellen Gravely'': 'You ransacked my hotel, captured my staff with that strange vacuum of yours...  And to top it all off, you '''catnapped''' my sweetie, my little darling... My precious Polterkitty!'}}

